{"title":"Career Roadmap · Product Designer","role":"Product Designer","summary":"A Product Designer in Toy & Game Design designs physical and interactive products that combine play, usability, safety, storytelling, aesthetics, materials and manufacturing. The role can cover toys, board games, educational products, collectibles, activity kits, children's products, interactive play systems and increasingly digital-physical experiences.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Toy & Game Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Approx. Years","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"2026–2027"},{"text":"Design, sketching, materials and play"}],[{"text":"Exploration"},{"text":"2027–2028"},{"text":"Toy/game concepts and prototyping"}],[{"text":"Product Development"},{"text":"2028–2029"},{"text":"User testing, CAD and manufacturing"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"2029–2030"},{"text":"Product Design Intern / Junior Designer"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Commercial toy/game products"}],[{"text":"Professional"},{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"End-to-end product ownership"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"2037–2040"},{"text":"Senior Designer / Design Lead"}],[{"text":"Strategic"},{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Design Manager / Creative Director"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Design & Play Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build fundamentals in industrial design and play design."},{"type":"h","text":"Design fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design principles"},{"text":"Form and proportion"},{"text":"Colour theory"},{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Visual hierarchy"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Visual storytelling"},{"text":"Design research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Toy and game fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Types of play"},{"text":"Age-appropriate design"},{"text":"Rules and mechanics"},{"text":"Reward systems"},{"text":"Challenge"},{"text":"Exploration"},{"text":"Social play"},{"text":"Imaginative play"},{"text":"Educational play"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sketching"},{"type":"p","text":"Practice:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product sketching"},{"text":"Perspective"},{"text":"Orthographic views"},{"text":"Exploded views"},{"text":"Concept sketches"},{"text":"Storyboards"},{"text":"Character/product ideation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Physical prototyping"},{"type":"p","text":"Experiment with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Paper"},{"text":"Cardboard"},{"text":"Foam"},{"text":"Wood"},{"text":"Clay"},{"text":"Fabric"},{"text":"Plastics"},{"text":"Recycled materials"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Proof of learning"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"20+ toy concepts"},{"text":"5 physical prototypes"},{"text":"2 board-game concepts"},{"text":"One educational toy"},{"text":"One fully documented design project"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Product Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Move from ideas toward usable products."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User research"},{"text":"Persona development"},{"text":"Play observation"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Anthropometrics"},{"text":"Product architecture"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Mechanisms"},{"text":"Basic manufacturing"},{"text":"Prototyping"}]},{"type":"h","text":"CAD"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn at least one strong 3D modelling workflow:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fusion"},{"text":"SolidWorks"},{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"Blender"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rendering"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"KeyShot"},{"text":"Blender rendering"},{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"Illustrator"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Game/product design"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Rules"},{"text":"Interaction"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Multiplayer/social interaction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"User testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Test prototypes with appropriate users and observe:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Understanding"},{"text":"Engagement"},{"text":"Confusion"},{"text":"Safety issues"},{"text":"Durability"},{"text":"Play duration"},{"text":"Repeat use"},{"text":"Accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Professional Product Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on commercialisation."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product development"},{"text":"Design for manufacturing"},{"text":"Design for assembly"},{"text":"Injection moulding basics"},{"text":"3D printing"},{"text":"CNC"},{"text":"Material selection"},{"text":"Cost awareness"},{"text":"Packaging"},{"text":"Branding"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Supplier communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Toy manufacturing"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Plastics"},{"text":"ABS"},{"text":"PP"},{"text":"PE"},{"text":"EVA"},{"text":"Silicone"},{"text":"Wood"},{"text":"Fabric"},{"text":"Magnets"},{"text":"Electronics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Material selection should always consider the intended user, durability and applicable safety requirements."},{"type":"h","text":"Safety"},{"type":"p","text":"For children's products, develop awareness of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mechanical hazards"},{"text":"Sharp edges"},{"text":"Small parts"},{"text":"Choking risks"},{"text":"Pinch points"},{"text":"Toxic materials"},{"text":"Flammability"},{"text":"Electrical safety"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Applicable toy/product safety standards vary by market, so designers should verify the current requirements for the target country before commercialisation."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Industry Readiness"