asingly support Product Designers with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Concept generation"},{"text":"Design variations"},{"text":"Market research"},{"text":"User research analysis"},{"text":"Generative form exploration"},{"text":"CAD assistance"},{"text":"Product visualisation"},{"text":"Packaging concepts"},{"text":"Playtesting analysis"},{"text":"Personalised learning experiences"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The designer still needs to make decisions about:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User needs"},{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Play value"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Cost"},{"text":"Emotional experience"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong future profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Product Design","Toy/Game Mechanics","CAD","Prototyping","User Research","AI","Manufacturing"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"2040–2046 Evolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The toy and game industry is likely to move increasingly toward physical-digital experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"Emerging areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-powered toys"},{"text":"Adaptive learning toys"},{"text":"Connected toys"},{"text":"Robotics-based toys"},{"text":"AR toys"},{"text":"VR experiences"},{"text":"Digital collectibles"},{"text":"Personalised educational products"},{"text":"Generative game systems"},{"text":"Sustainable/circular toys"},{"text":"Assistive and inclusive play products"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The Product Designer will increasingly design ecosystems rather than individual objects."},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Physical toy","mobile application","AI assistant","digital game","learning platform"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product Design"},{"text":"Toy Design"},{"text":"Game Design"},{"text":"Human-Centred Design"},{"text":"Design Research"},{"text":"Play Design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SolidWorks/Fusion"},{"text":"Rhino/Blender"},{"text":"KeyShot"},{"text":"3D printing"},{"text":"Basic electronics"},{"text":"Arduino/ESP32"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Prototyping"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Foam"},{"text":"Wood"},{"text":"Plastic"},{"text":"Clay"},{"text":"3D printing"},{"text":"Laser cutting"},{"text":"Functional prototypes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Business"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Costing"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Supply chain"},{"text":"Packaging"},{"text":"Product lifecycle"},{"text":"Market research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted design"},{"text":"AR/VR"},{"text":"Smart toys"},{"text":"Robotics"},{"text":"Generative design"},{"text":"Sustainable/circular design"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"p","text":"Design Foundations → Toy/Game Ideation"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2"},{"type":"p","text":"Product Design → CAD + Prototyping"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3"},{"type":"p","text":"User Testing → Manufacturing + Commercial Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4"},{"type":"p","text":"Complete Product Portfolio → Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Years 5–7"},{"type":"p","text":"Junior Product Designer → Product Designer"},{"type":"h","text":"Years 8–12"},{"type":"p","text":"Product Designer → Senior Product Designer"},{"type":"h","text":"Years 12–16"},{"type":"p","text":"Senior → Lead Product Designer"},{"type":"h","text":"Years 16–20"},{"type":"p","text":"Design Lead → Design Manager / Creative Director"},{"type":"h","text":"Best Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong B.Des Toy & Game Design graduate targeting Product Design should ideally have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong product-design fundamentals"},{"text":"Toy and game mechanics knowledge"},{"text":"Excellent sketching"},{"text":"CAD proficiency"},{"text":"Strong physical prototyping ability"},{"text":"3D-printing experience"},{"text":"User research and playtesting"},{"text":"Manufacturing awareness"},{"text":"Product safety awareness"},{"text":"Packaging understanding"},{"text":"4–6 polished product projects"},{"text":"At least 2 functional prototypes"},{"text":"One complete toy/game product"},{"text":"One educational/STEM product"},{"text":"Industry internship"},{"text":"Professional product-design portfolio"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Ideal profile","text":"A Product Designer who combines toy and game mechanics, human-centred design, physical prototyping, CAD, manufacturing, user testing and emerging digital technologies to create safe, engaging and commercially viable play products."}]}]}